IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cta-importer`

-- Customs Tariff Act 1995 -- worked cases, from the seat of the traveller or small importer. Every assertion is a claim
-- about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand from the deposited text
-- (Compilation No. 100), reading the rate in the third column of each Schedule 3 line and each Schedule 4 item, never copied
-- from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL; no scenario raised this Act.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The general rate in Schedule 3.
#ASSERT `The general rate for my goods` `8471.30.00 a laptop or other portable computer of 10 kg or less` EQUALS `answered` 0
#ASSERT `The general rate for my goods` `8517.13.00 a smartphone` EQUALS `answered` 0
#ASSERT `The general rate for my goods` `6109.10.00 a cotton T-shirt, singlet or vest, knitted or crocheted` EQUALS `answered` 5
#ASSERT `The general rate for my goods` `4202.21.00 a leather handbag` EQUALS `answered` 5
#ASSERT `The general rate for my goods` `9503.00.20 a doll representing a human being, or its parts and accessories` EQUALS `answered` 5
#ASSERT `The general rate for my goods` `8711.60.00 an electric bicycle, scooter or motorcycle` EQUALS `answered` 5
#ASSERT `The general rate for my goods` `8703.80.11 a used electric passenger car` EQUALS `answered` 5
#ASSERT `The general rate for my goods` `8703.80.12 a new electric passenger car valued below the fuel-efficient car limit` EQUALS `answered` 0
#ASSERT `The general rate for my goods` `8703.80.19 another electric passenger car` EQUALS `answered` 5
#ASSERT `The general rate for my goods` `another classification` EQUALS `not covered` `only nine representative Schedule 3 classifications are encoded; look up the rate for this classification in Schedule 3`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The rate by origin (s 16). Inputs after the classification: origin; the FTA schedule lists it; its rate; also Canadian.
-- A leather handbag with no preference: 5% (s 16(1)(a)).
#ASSERT `The rate for my goods by origin` `4202.21.00 a leather handbag` `none of these (no preference)` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 5
-- The same handbag, New Zealand originating goods: no NZ rate set, so Free (s 16(1)(b)(ii)).
#ASSERT `The rate for my goods by origin` `4202.21.00 a leather handbag` `New Zealand originating goods` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 0
-- Chinese originating goods, the China schedule not listing the heading: Free (s 16(1)(r)(ii)).
#ASSERT `The rate for my goods by origin` `4202.21.00 a leather handbag` `originating goods of a free trade agreement partner (Singapore, US, Thailand, Peru, Chile, ASEAN-Australia-NZ, Pacific Islands, TPP, Malaysia, Indonesia, Korea, India, Japan, China, Hong Kong, RCEP, UK or UAE)` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 0
-- Hypothetically, a free trade schedule that lists the heading at 2%: 2% (s 16(1)(ja)-(v)(i)).
#ASSERT `The rate for my goods by origin` `4202.21.00 a leather handbag` `originating goods of a free trade agreement partner (Singapore, US, Thailand, Peru, Chile, ASEAN-Australia-NZ, Pacific Islands, TPP, Malaysia, Indonesia, Korea, India, Japan, China, Hong Kong, RCEP, UK or UAE)` TRUE 2 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 2
-- A doll made in Canada: CA:Free (s 16(1)(d)(i)); a handbag made in Canada: no CA rate, so the general 5% (s 16(1)(d)(ii)).
#ASSERT `The rate for my goods by origin` `9503.00.20 a doll representing a human being, or its parts and accessories` `the produce or manufacture of Canada` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 0
#ASSERT `The rate for my goods by origin` `4202.21.00 a leather handbag` `the produce or manufacture of Canada` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 5
-- A used electric car from Japan with no preference claimed: 5%.
#ASSERT `The rate for my goods by origin` `8703.80.11 a used electric passenger car` `none of these (no preference)` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` 5
-- Goods both a hypothetical FTA partner's at 2% and Canada's at Free: the least duty, Free (s 16(5)).
#ASSERT `The rate for my goods by origin` `8703.80.19 another electric passenger car` `originating goods of a free trade agreement partner (Singapore, US, Thailand, Peru, Chile, ASEAN-Australia-NZ, Pacific Islands, TPP, Malaysia, Indonesia, Korea, India, Japan, China, Hong Kong, RCEP, UK or UAE)` TRUE 2 TRUE EQUALS `answered` 0
-- An electric bike from a Developing Country: not covered (the DCS 4% needs the regulations' list).
#ASSERT `The rate for my goods by origin` `8711.60.00 an electric bicycle, scooter or motorcycle` `the produce of Papua New Guinea, a Forum Island Country, or a Developing or Least Developed Country` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the preferences for Papua New Guinea, Forum Island, Developing and Least Developed Countries are not encoded (their countries are listed in regulations not deposited)`
#ASSERT `The rate for my goods by origin` `another classification` `none of these (no preference)` FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `only nine representative Schedule 3 classifications are encoded; look up the rate for this classification in Schedule 3`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Concessions (Schedule 4, s 18). Inputs: the item; described (and prescribed); the rate otherwise applying; Canadian.
-- A 1965 Mustang (30 years or more), otherwise 5%: item 36, Free.
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 36: a passenger car, or certain utilities, 30 or more years old` TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the item applies, and the goods are Free (ss 8, 18(1), Schedule 4)`
-- A used electric car prescribed by by-law under item 37 (5%), otherwise 5% under 8703.80.11: no less duty, so item 37 does
-- not apply (s 18(1)).
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 37: a used or second-hand passenger car` TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: the item gives no less duty than the rate that otherwise applies, so it does not apply and that rate stands (s 18(1))`
-- A used petrol car otherwise at a hypothetical higher rate of 10%: item 37 applies at 5%.
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 37: a used or second-hand passenger car` TRUE 10 FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: item 37 applies, at 5% of the value (ss 8, 18(1), Schedule 4)`
-- The same car, made in Canada, otherwise 10%: item 37's CA rate is Free.
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 37: a used or second-hand passenger car` TRUE 10 TRUE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the item applies, and the goods are Free (ss 8, 18(1), Schedule 4)`
-- A leather handbag she took overseas and brought back unaltered (item 17, prescribed by by-law), otherwise 5%: Free.
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 17: goods I exported and brought back unaltered` TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the item applies, and the goods are Free (ss 8, 18(1), Schedule 4)`
-- A smartphone replaced under warranty (item 18): already Free under Schedule 3, so the item gives no less duty.
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 18: goods repaired or replaced free under warranty or a safety recall` TRUE 0 FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: the item gives no less duty than the rate that otherwise applies, so it does not apply and that rate stands (s 18(1))`
-- Her grandmother's jewellery inherited while she lived in Perth, the Collector satisfied (item 24), otherwise 5%: Free.
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 24: goods I inherited, not for sale or trade` TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the item applies, and the goods are Free (ss 8, 18(1), Schedule 4)`
-- Low-value goods under item 26 that are not of a kind the by-law prescribes.
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 26: goods of low value` FALSE 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` `no: the goods are not described in the item (or not prescribed by the by-law it needs) (s 8(1))`
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 28: an aid or appliance for a person with a disability` TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the item applies, and the goods are Free (ss 8, 18(1), Schedule 4)`
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 25: a trophy, decoration, medallion or certificate won or awarded overseas` TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS `answered` `yes: the item applies, and the goods are Free (ss 8, 18(1), Schedule 4)`
-- The passenger concession is the Customs Act baseline's.
#ASSERT `Does a concession apply to my goods` `item 15: goods brought in as a passenger` TRUE 5 FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `the passenger concession (Schedule 4 item 15) is answered by the Customs Act 1901 baseline, not restated here`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The duty (s 9). A $1,200 leather handbag at 5%: $60; a $40,000 used electric car at 5%: $2,000; a laptop, Free: nil.
#ASSERT `The duty on my goods` 5 1200 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `The duty on my goods` 5 40000 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `The duty on my goods` 0 2500 EQUALS 0
